Main customer sales document that records, validates, and tracks customer orders from quotation to delivery and invoicing.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Quotations → Sales Orders conversion
Customer order management with lines, prices, discounts, and taxes
Automatic creation of deliveries (stock.picking) and invoices (account.move)
Sales forecasting, margin analysis, and order fulfillment
Upsell, cross-sell, and product configurator
Multi-step approval workflows
Dropshipping, MTO, and service orders

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread + activity.mixin)
Key Fields:
name (sequenced: SOxxxx), state (draft/sent/sale/done/cancel)
partner_id → res.partner (required), partner_invoice_id, partner_shipping_id
date_order, commitment_date, validity_date
amount_untaxed, amount_tax, amount_total
One2many: order_line → sale.order.line
pricelist_id, payment_term_id, fiscal_position_id, team_id, user_id (salesperson)
warehouse_id, picking_ids, invoice_ids

Critical Hooks: action_confirm, action_quotation_send, _prepare_invoice, _create_picking, onchange_partner_id, _compute_amount
Security: sales_team.group_sale_salesman + company + own documents rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
sales order, SO, quotation, customer order, sale order, sales quotation, sales confirmation, customer PO, order confirmation, sale document, sales pipeline, draft quotation, confirmed sales order, pending order, awaiting confirmation, cancelled order, order status, sales order state, to invoice, fully invoiced, open sales order
Related Models (most joined):

sale.order.line (child lines — most important)
res.partner (customer)
product.product / product.template
stock.picking (deliveries)
account.move (invoices)
sale.order.line, crm.lead (opportunity link)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
sale.order is Odoo’s core sales document model storing customer orders with partner_id, order lines, totals, state, and dates. It drives quotation workflow, order confirmation, automatic delivery and invoice creation, margin calculation, and serves as the central hub connecting Sales, Inventory, Accounting, and CRM modules.